//:: cases TC_CA_7_IntentionalOuterInnerStillFires
//:: tools silicon
//:: verdict Fail

// TC-CA-7: assert false suppresses the outer warning but NOT inner branches.
//
// When isIntentionallyDead(body) is true, instrumentBody calls dispatch(body)
// directly without inserting an outer refute false.  dispatch(body) still
// recursively instruments everything inside the body — inner branches get
// their own refute false checks.
//
// Since the whole outer branch is dead (requires x > 0, condition x < 0),
// the inner if (x > 5) is also in a contradictory state.  Its refute false
// fires, and because there is no outer blame in scope (the outer was intentional),
// the inner blame has ancestorFired = () => false — so it reports deadBranch.
//
// Summary:
//   outer if (x < 0): assert false → no outer warning (intentional)
//   inner if (x > 5): no assert false → its check fires → deadBranch reported
//
// Expected: Fail — inner branch fires despite outer being marked intentional.
// To silence all warnings the developer must mark inner branches intentional too.
requires x > 0;
void f(int x) {
    if (x > 5) {
        assert false; // outer intentional — no outer deadBranch
        if (x > 5) {  // inner dead — NOT suppressed; fires independently
            x = x + 1;
        }
    }
}
